<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladimír Mečiar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladimír Mečiar is a Slovak politician who led the Movement for a Democratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and was prime minister of Slovakia three times between 1990 and 1998. After winning the 1992 elections in Slovakia, he negotiated the dissolution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaclav-klaus">Václav Klaus</a>. His later governments were criticised for authoritarian methods, which delayed Slovakia's entry into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladimir-meciar.jpg" alt="Vladimír Mečiar" width="200" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Péter Kamocsai · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vladimir_Meciar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
